<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany: Could regional polls force Friedrich Merz to step down?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eff91eba2d3f308b4b4793db669e5e52109d2c0eb16ae415e66c5363ac8555e4</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T10:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-could-regional-polls-froce-friedrich-merz-to-step-down" /><summary type="html">Polling is underway in the German capital Berlin and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania for regional elections. Both elections are seen as a test for Germany's centre-right Chancellor Friedrich Merz. He has already scheduled a crisis meeting and decided to skip this week's UN General Assembly to deal with the potential fallout. Could he be forced to step down based on the election’s results? Details and analysis by Yann Wernert, senior policy fellow at the Jacques Delors Centre in Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine hits Russia with major drone attack, targetting refinery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22bad6cca95b5decb59d896c35d4da466883c2852e04742770039401c8de2344</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T10:24:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hits-russia-with-major-drone-attack-targetting-refinery" /><summary type="html">In Russia, voters are on the third and final day of casting ballots in the country's first wartime parliamentary election. Despite the voting however, Ukraine carried out what Moscow described as the "largest ever" drone attack on the Russian capital. Kyiv reportedly fired over 1.000 drones at the country, leaving two dead in the Moscow region and inflicting damage upon an oil refinery. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.</summary></entry><entry><title>US and Denmark reach Greenland security deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1c6d427227dea0d8a6f0b01ad9b350424fe915a7837234b8554db5d33a58a6d</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:40:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-greenland-security-deal" /><summary type="html">The US and Denmark have announced a deal on Greenland's security, resolving a diplomatic dispute sparked by President Donald Trump when he threatened to seize the semi-autonomous territory. The exact terms of the deal remain uncertain but it seems Denmark will maintain its sovereignty while the US will be able to develop a significant military presence on the island, and ban their adversaries from building their own bases on the island. Details by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will German's far right party AfD win over two more regions?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f90feb4ec09bd444f227f77d550d221a99fa4b9f8b3ecfc68a692c4146cd8033</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:35:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/will-german-s-far-right-party-afd-win-over-two-more-regions" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the far-right AfD won its first major regional election in Germany, two more eastern states vote this Sunday. Polls have just opened in the capital, Berlin, and the largely rural state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Berlin, Jörg Taszman.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Russian election enters final day after Kyiv targets Moscow in massive drone attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1240ea456ea5e652b2d85a2030c0bc91268a8816313d9626aa6aa31d3fd04df6</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T05:16:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-live-russian-election-enters-final-day-in-shadow-of-war-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine launched what Moscow’s Mayor Sergei Sobyanin described on Sunday as the “largest ever” attack on the Russian capital, killing two people and damaging part of an oil refinery. The major attack comes on the third and final day of voting in Russia’s first wartime parliamentary election. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Merz under pressure as two more German states hold elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b55dc07fe60ca1d9917aa4b3f1135414a6d4e2a9d634ffc88586cf41142ba95b</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T01:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260920-germans-vote-in-elections-threatening-fresh-blow-to-merz" /><summary type="html">Germans began voting Sunday in two closely watched state elections that could deliver fresh gains for the far-right and far-left, piling pressure on Chancellor Friedrich Merz as he struggles with low approval ratings and tensions within his governing coalition.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Greenland Deal: Greenland: A Trump Win or Danish Masterclass?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fadcddbe4c02921d441616c5f4f1593e0de9d2d70726e203ab2f47be0c506223</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:37:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260919-greenland-deal-greenland-a-trump-win-or-danish-masterclass--49777f9c5bf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260919-greenland-deal-greenland-a-trump-win-or-danish-masterclass" /><summary type="html">Is there a resolution on Greenland?
 
President Trump’s pressure campaign began in December 2024, right after he won re-election, when he began talking about the need for U.S. ownership and control of the semi-autonomous Danish territory.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Germany braces for key state elections where far right party AfD seeks another breakthrough</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dfb378b2c90795ca68f245d1fdfa782b8424be1e1644feee5e353b23e65b5dd</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:28:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-braces-for-key-state-elections-where-far-right-party-afd-seeks-another-breakthrough--ced0cb860143.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-braces-for-key-state-elections-where-far-right-party-afd-seeks-another-breakthrough" /><summary type="html">Germany is gearing up for two more pivotal state elections on Sunday: in the capital Berlin and in the largely rural region of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania. All eyes are on the far-right AfD, which after recording its best ever result in the recent Saxony-Anhalt elections, is hoping to once again make sweeping gains. The anti-immigration party's surging popularity is proving challenging for Chancellor Friedrich Merz and both elections are expected to further test his leadership. Story by Eliza Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin says Europe is 'preparing for war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ae884b7d63f8dfe282a221ffe18d66035aee8a9ddd4dc413a4fd7aa30bdbb0e</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:04:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/putin-says-europe-is-preparing-for-war--d7dfde1b7973.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/putin-says-europe-is-preparing-for-war" /><summary type="html">As the West continues to denounce Russian aggression in Ukraine and to support Kyiv with a host of economic and military measures, Russian President Vladimir Putin says that Nato is expanding its reach and influence with the intention of preparing for war with Russia. Analysis by Dr Alexander Titov, lecturer in Modern European History at Queen's University Belfast in the UK.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian children learn ancient warrior skills amid modern war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01d2fa457f1745ec04a781ef9b91a95c7196c3b24197ce3c973bc15b504b2801</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:21:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-children-learn-ancient-warrior-skills-amid-modern-war--fde9fce1fd13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukrainian-children-learn-ancient-warrior-skills-amid-modern-war" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian children are learning the skills of 17th-century Cossack warriors – the communities that played a central role in Ukraine history, known for their military skills and horsemanship. But for these students, it is more than a history lesson. It is a chance to escape the reality of growing up during war. Story by Charlotte Lam.</summary></entry><entry><title>Did Trump really obtain 'permanent control' over Greenland?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2340173008cecd94c0af6546ffc8c773fcdc3845b6d1af066f4a33c9161b7df5</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:07:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/did-trump-really-obtain-permanent-control-over-greenland--a125835d55d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/did-trump-really-obtain-permanent-control-over-greenland" /><summary type="html">Danish Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen has described a deal for the US to develop a significant military presence on Greenland, as 'a good agreement'. US President Donald Trump announced the deal on Friday, after he spent months seeking to acquire Greenland, citing threats from Russia and China, and even raised the possibility of military action. Story by Charlotte Hughes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany cuts energy tax to lower petrol prices as Merz faces state key elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:689a0a06107cd793ac04259ff2fa83022604e003e21dd57052922bb36b8432ed</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T10:05:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-germany-cuts-energy-tax-to-lower-soaring-petrol-prices--8471e3f9a878.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-germany-cuts-energy-tax-to-lower-soaring-petrol-prices" /><summary type="html">Germany will cut taxes on gasoline and diesel by about 17 cents a litre from October, the government said Friday. The move comes ahead of state elections in the capital Berlin and the northeastern state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania where Chancellor Friedrich Merz's conservative Christian Democrats are expected to be soundly defeated.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain's police launch operation to clear migrants off Ceuta beach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e561e9b43ba582665e508611a17a10504b796e8880d6e35f7354d2d4bc5c6520</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:57:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-police-launch-operation-to-clear-migrants-off-ceuta-beach--69bde6533cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-police-launch-operation-to-clear-migrants-off-ceuta-beach" /><summary type="html">Police on Friday moved hundreds of migrants from the beaches of Ceuta to a temporary camp in the Spanish enclave's port area. The police operation takes place weeks after a record influx of people into Spain's North African tiny territory. During the transfer, the police struggled to contain crowds jostling to get a place at the new tented site. The policing takes place with the issue of migration centre stage in Spain's political debate. Details by Nicholas Rushworth.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s Macron warns of Russian ‘hybrid’ attacks, seeks to step up energy defence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a89fe8ccea0d9c61a928b9304b0190814db53e120248d7f8fcca853e78899f31</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:52:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-warns-of-russian-hybrid-attacks-seeks-to-step-up-energy-defence--04c7e0a32971.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-macron-warns-of-russian-hybrid-attacks-seeks-to-step-up-energy-defence" /><summary type="html">Just months before France's presidential election, rising fuel costs due to the wars in Iran and Ukraine have pushed the nation to the verge of crisis. In an attempt to address public anger and energy threats, French President Emmanuel Macron gathered the nation's major party presidential candidates at the presidential palace. But the main takeaway from this meeting was perhaps Macron's warning about Russian "hybrid attacks"... what exactly does he mean and how serious is the threat? Details and analysis by Richard Werly, France and Europe correspondent for Blick.</summary></entry><entry><title>Princess Diana's iconic 'revenge dress' goes to auction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfd1f6e9beb0d59c22b0f51ccc21bccd114a65b1f768f76816587773e93a723e</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:57:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/princess-diana-s-iconic-revenge-dress-goes-to-auction--d035f6b47dc6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/princess-diana-s-iconic-revenge-dress-goes-to-auction" /><summary type="html">As the worldwide release of Diana Spencer’s brother’s book prompts a reaction from King Charles and the British Crown, another piece of Diana's legacy is making headlines – the iconic little black dress, worn by the then Princess of Wales, is going under the hammer. Better known as the "Revenge Dress", it would go on to inspire generations of women.</summary></entry><entry><title>US and Denmark reach deal on Greenland, Trump claims 'permanent control' over island</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26d924c2bc848d1da32c42352771421d7fcb4b97ffdd613fe20f16e6d55d64f3</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:48:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-deal-on-greenland-trump-claims-permanent-control-over-island--23916a8df746.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-and-denmark-reach-deal-on-greenland-trump-claims-permanent-control-over-island" /><summary type="html">Not so long ago, inhabitants of Greenland feared that the US was preparing to invade, after US President Donald Trump repeatedly claimed the US wanted to control the Arctic territory. But Trump now says he has struck a deal with Denmark to give Washington "permanent control" over Greenland's security, while ensuring the territory remains firmly in the hands of Denmark. Denmark and Greenland have both hailed the deal, but its exact terms remain unclear. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Washington, Fraser Jackson.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia reports cyberattacks as parliamentary vote enters second day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e926c09cb41217c78638469800577e94c0654d0f87f0c175e9b45a3101dbba57</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T05:24:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-ukraine-live-russian-strike-on-apartment-building-in-ukraine-s-sumy-kills-at-least-two--a8179e07ef68.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260919-ukraine-live-russian-strike-on-apartment-building-in-ukraine-s-sumy-kills-at-least-two" /><summary type="html">Russia said Saturday that its electronic voting system in Moscow had come under “powerful” cyberattacks overnight, as parliamentary elections entered their second day. Russian President Vladimir Putin on Friday accused Ukraine of seeking to “hinder” the vote, a claim Kyiv has not publicly addressed. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Denmark hails Greenland deal with Trump respecting ‘red lines’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d36d32f5cf124fbc2005f00fd7614825ef01964a5d7ab942be17212ae7d8db81</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T22:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-denmark-hails-binding-greenland-deal-with-trump--ac85e1153654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-denmark-hails-binding-greenland-deal-with-trump" /><summary type="html">Denmark on Saturday welcomed a deal announced by President Donald Trump that bolsters the US military presence in Greenland and limits its adversaries from investing or having a military presence on the Arctic territory. Danish Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen said the deal respects the "red lines" of sovereignty and "the Greenlandic people's right to self-determination".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says US, Denmark reach deal to expand military presence in Greenland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4880e22081861438b49bedda6fc88975b4a1b8230c39802112cb440c6f5173ce</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T22:18:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-greenland-denmark-us-deal-un-general-assembly--57e97d7b07ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-greenland-denmark-us-deal-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said on Friday he had reached a deal with Denmark to expand the US military presence in Greenland, while respecting Danish and Greenlandic sovereignty. Denmark said the agreement would be signed next week during the UN General Assembly but still requires parliamentary approval.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden's centre-left leader Andersson tasked with forming government after election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28ca148ceb254ed8c42faf8b3da8d03cdb068b1f0896f8b73fcb548dbd4366e5</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T16:01:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-sweden-s-centre-left-leader-andersson-tasked-with-forming-government-after-election--275f5e18284a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-sweden-s-centre-left-leader-andersson-tasked-with-forming-government-after-election" /><summary type="html">Sweden's parliament speaker on Friday tasked opposition leader Magdalena Andersson with forming a government after an election gave the left-wing bloc a narrow majority, setting the stage for difficult coalition talks. Andersson, a former prime minister, must bridge deep differences between four parties, with the centre party ruling out a government that includes the left in cabinet.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>We’re ideally placed to chair EU budget negotiations, says Irish Minister of State</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a57a88bc18e6ae3220a2d5e0e2370cb002f31cdf0aae10334b76b693daf5873</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:17:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-we-re-ideally-placed-to-chair-eu-budget-negotiations-says-irish-minister-of-state--ba023e43e00e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-we-re-ideally-placed-to-chair-eu-budget-negotiations-says-irish-minister-of-state" /><summary type="html">Ireland is managing a jam-packed agenda as the current holder of the rotating presidency of the EU. We caught up with the country’s Minister of State for European Affairs, Thomas Byrne, who was in Strasbourg for the 2026 State of the Union speech and debate with EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen. We discussed key points from that address, such as a proposed ban on social media access for children, which Ireland is keen to push forward with during its EU presidency.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ursula von der Leyen’s sixth State of the Union speech: A grand sweep, but thin on details?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ff478f9da84a706b06dc396721c7d06bbf7caef29d001ef73d96c2f48b9d9cb</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:17:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-ursula-von-der-leyen-s-sixth-state-of-the-union-speech-a-grand-sweep-but-thin-on-details--4838abbf8b86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260918-ursula-von-der-leyen-s-sixth-state-of-the-union-speech-a-grand-sweep-but-thin-on-details" /><summary type="html">In this episode, we debrief one of the key annual events in the EU calendar: the State of the Union speech. It was Ursula von der Leyen’s sixth such address as President of the European Commission, and the second State of the Union speech of her second mandate.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Police move hundreds of migrants still in Ceuta off beaches in Spanish enclave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7f59f82bc7e081c7dcc5e57e0173de7cb2d63f5b4eb4d32f6fbc6593efaa742</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:51:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-police-move-hundreds-of-migrants-still-in-ceuta-off-beaches-in-spanish-enclave--58be737d34d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-police-move-hundreds-of-migrants-still-in-ceuta-off-beaches-in-spanish-enclave" /><summary type="html">Spanish police in Ceuta on Friday morning started moving hundreds of migrants from the beaches of the Spanish enclave to a new tented area. Several thousand migrants remain in Ceuta after tens of thousands of people crossed the border with Morocco in late July.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia seizes assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French firms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb28a23ff19578d214962884cf319bdbbce9ab2440704820c04b220c56f3c5f2</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:11:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-seizes-assets-of-swiss-food-giant-nestle-and-three-french-firms--b07bee861c7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-seizes-assets-of-swiss-food-giant-nestle-and-three-french-firms" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin signed a decree Thursday to take control of the Russian assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French groups, citing hostile actions by "unfriendly" countries. France responded by calling on Russia to "reverse this decision".  While most Western companies sold their Russian operations and holdings after Moscow launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine, the Kremlin has since made it difficult for firms to leave the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia votes in parliamentary election as war in Ukraine drags on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3202f875ce1a87340d918594bb207b64414639a7ae780a4b3119160ee569035</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T05:38:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-votes-in-wartime-parliamentary-election-set-to-secure-the-kremlin-power--bb8eff96fe52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-votes-in-wartime-parliamentary-election-set-to-secure-the-kremlin-power" /><summary type="html">Polls opened in Russia's Far East on Friday as the country began three days of voting for its parliamentary election, the first since Moscow launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine. The Kremlin's main party, United Russia, is poised to keep its grip on power alongside other parties aligned with President Vladimir Putin, as the only party that criticised the war was removed from the ballot.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia targets Kyiv with new missile attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e3827eb4e7e2621fbbba782f289839e0622f2d8594c7db59e68139decc328c2</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T03:16:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-live-voting-begins-in-russia-s-parliamentary-elections--3c581f101d42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-live-voting-begins-in-russia-s-parliamentary-elections" /><summary type="html">The ⁠Ukrainian ​capital ​Kyiv again came under fire from ‌Russian ⁠missiles on ​Friday, ‌Mayor ‌Vitali Klitschko ​said, with witnesses confirming they could hear explosions in the capital. Earlier, Moscow struck four Ukrainian cargo vessels in the Black Sea, Russian state media said. The latest attacks unfolded as Russians headed to the polls for the country's first parliamentary election since the start of the war. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'major progress' made towards US military base in Poland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:335bc5dde81594bc397937184b91f9c6586c02b289327b4a3b22039df9bf7da2</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T01:04:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-trump-says-major-progress-made-toward-us-military-base-in-poland--fed731656a65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-trump-says-major-progress-made-toward-us-military-base-in-poland" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said that Washington and Warsaw were making "major progress" towards establishing a US military base in Poland, potentially giving the United States a permanent military foothold on NATO's eastern flank even as his administration reviews its broader troop presence in Europe.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French police officer arrested over suspected far-right terror plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6c6da4f9562bbd2b952c77b29870d620352e5a82d476ee3ca97210091f4e681</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T22:29:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-french-police-officer-arrested-over-suspected-far-right-terror-plot--418a088cb674.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-french-police-officer-arrested-over-suspected-far-right-terror-plot" /><summary type="html">A French police officer who allegedly adheres to a "violent radical far-right ideology" has been arrested on suspicion of plotting attacks against state interests and manufacturing 3D-printed weapons, sources told AFP Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The Ceuta effect: how far will Europe's anti-migrant backlash go?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d448130064f09643ba87962dc7c8f785e22a5e8797517b2e89ebc32cb47b7053</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T18:16:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260917-the-ceuta-effect-how-far-will-europe-s-anti-migrant-backlash-go--f55ba423d1ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260917-the-ceuta-effect-how-far-will-europe-s-anti-migrant-backlash-go" /><summary type="html">As the United States threatens Europe with more tariffs and eyes Greenland, Russia tests the continent’s resolve over Ukraine and the planet overheats, where do citizens feel the biggest threat is coming from? In her Wednesday state of the Union speech, the European Commission president Ursula von der Leyen went big on manning the borders, suggesting new tools to better deal with migration. This comes against in a context of Ceuta where over two days in July, tens of thousands of mostly Moroccans overran Spain’s North African enclave.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>English village holds symbolic vote to leave UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aba217957614bf6104dcd2f93c7abb00bbeb5bdb2e4388c16adacfe74e663eb</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T15:17:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/english-village-holds-symbolic-vote-to-leave-uk--01fb1662a4dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/english-village-holds-symbolic-vote-to-leave-uk" /><summary type="html">A village in Oxfordshire has held a symbolic referendum to leave the United Kingdom in protest against government plans to house up to 1,200 asylum seekers at a nearby military base. While the vote has no legal force, it highlights wider tensions over the UK's asylum policy and migration debate.</summary></entry></feed>
